Creating an advanced notepad app with syntax highlighting and other features in a single HTML file involves using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Below is a simple implementation that includes syntax highlighting, line numbers, and a basic toolbar with features like saving and loading files. This example uses the CodeMirror library for syntax highlighting.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Advanced Notepad</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/codemirror.min.css">
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            height: 100vh;
        }
        #toolbar {
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            padding: 10px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
        }
        #editor {
            flex-grow: 1;
        }
        button {
            margin-right: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="toolbar">
        <div>
            <button onclick="saveFile()">Save</button>
            <button onclick="loadFile()">Load</button>
        </div>
        <div>
            <button onclick="toggleTheme()">Toggle Theme</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <textarea id="editor"></textarea>

    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/codemirror.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.5/mode/javascript/javascript.min.js"></script>
    <script>
        const editor = CodeMirror.fromTextArea(document.getElementById('editor'), {
            lineNumbers: true,
            mode: "javascript",
            theme: "default"
        });

        function saveFile() {
            const blob = new Blob([editor.getValue()], { type: 'text/plain' });
            const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            const a = document.createElement('a');
            a.href = url;
            a.download = 'document.txt';
            a.click();
            URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
        }

        function loadFile() {
            const input = document.createElement('input');
            input.type = 'file';
            input.accept = '.txt';
            input.onchange = e => {
                const file = e.target.files[0];
                const reader = new FileReader();
                reader.onload = event => {
                    editor.setValue(event.target.result);
                };
                reader.readAsText(file);
            };
            input.click();
        }

        function toggleTheme() {
            const currentTheme = editor.getOption('theme');
            const newTheme = currentTheme === 'default' ? 'monokai' : 'default';
            editor.setOption('theme', newTheme);
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Features Included:
1. **Syntax Highlighting**: Using CodeMirror to highlight JavaScript syntax.
2. **Line Numbers**: Displayed on the left side of the editor.
3. **Save and Load**: Save the content to a `.txt` file and load content from a `.txt` file.
4. **Theme Toggle**: Switch between light and dark themes.

### How to Use:
- **Save**: Click the "Save" button to download the current content as a text file.
- **Load**: Click the "Load" button to upload a text file and display its content in the editor.
- **Toggle Theme**: Click the "Toggle Theme" button to switch between light and dark themes.

### Note:
- This example uses the CodeMirror library for syntax highlighting. You can extend it to support more languages by including additional modes from CodeMirror.
